{"id": 45, "ts": 1781701879.5247004, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "I agree with my earlier inclination toward Candidate\u202fC and, in fact, the new confirmation that C is \u201cknown to be\u202f100\u202f% reliable\u201d strengthens that position. Operational reliability is a cornerstone for long\u2011distance flights, and this explicit evidence now puts C on equal footing with B\u2019s \u201cvery conscientious\u201d label, but with a concrete reliability record. Combined with C\u2019s proven decision quality (\u201ccan make correct decisions quickly\u201d) and his ability to foster a positive crew atmosphere, C now covers three of the most safety\u2011critical criteria: reliability, decision quality, and crew cooperation. The remaining unknown is stress resilience, but the lack of any evidence of B\u2019s decision\u2011making under pressure is a larger safety gap than C\u2019s unverified stress handling. Therefore, I maintain my provisional recommendation for **Candidate\u202fC** as the best overall fit."}
