{"id": 50, "ts": 1781701940.8850713, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "I appreciate the thorough comparison of B and C, but I\u2019m now leaning toward **Candidate\u202fC** as the stronger overall fit. The notes give us concrete evidence that C is \u201cknown to be\u202f100\u202f% reliable,\u201d which directly satisfies the operational\u2011reliability criterion, and that he \u201ccan make correct decisions quickly,\u201d addressing the critical decision\u2011quality requirement for long\u2011haul flights. Moreover, C \u201ccreates a positive atmosphere with his crew,\u201d indicating solid crew\u2011cooperation\u2014a safety\u2011critical factor that B lacks, given his \u201cuncooperative\u201d and \u201cgrumpy\u201d behavior. While we have no explicit observations of C\u2019s stress resilience, the absence of any evidence for B\u2019s decision quality under pressure is a larger safety gap; a pilot who cannot be trusted to make rapid, correct decisions in a crisis poses a higher risk than one whose stress handling is unrecorded but can be developed through training. Therefore, based on the available evidence, I would recommend Candidate\u202fC."}
